      "text": "To determine the month in which the batteries will be changed the 25th time, we need to consider the pattern of the change cycles and adjust the given year accordingly. Here is the step-by-step solution:\n\n1. **Identify the cycle of battery changes:**\n   Every 5 months, Hal changes the batteries.\n\n2. **Determine the total number of cycles in 25 changes:**\n   Since he changes the batteries every 5 months, after 25 changes, the total number of cycles is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{25}{5} = 5 \\text{ cycles}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the day of the month when the 25th change occurs:**\n   The first change occurs in May. To find the day of the month for the 25th change, we need to calculate:\n   \\[\n   25 \\times 5 = 125 \\text{ months}\n   \\]\n   Since there are 31 days in May, June, and July, we need to find the day of the month within these months.\n\n   - **May:** From May 1 to May 5, there are 5 days (1, 2, 3, 4, 5).\n   - **June:** From June 1 to June 5, there are 5 days (1, 2, 3, 4, 5).\n   - **July:** From July 1 to July 5, there are 5 days (1, 2, 3, 4, 5).\n\n   Since 125 months span 125 / 31 = 4 full years plus an additional 2 months (since 125 = 4 * 365 + 2, we subtract the days from 365 and add the additional 2 months).\n\n   Therefore, the day of the month for the 125th day is:\n   \\[\n   125 \\mod 31 = 2 \\text{ days into June}\n   \\]\n   So, the 125th day is in June.\n\nTherefore, the batteries will be changed the 25th time in \\boxed{June}.",
